      "writtenOn": "2017-11-15T17:08:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we are thinking too much into this than what I originally intended when I submitted this patch. My intention of the patch was just enable/disable TLS via a configuration with all other parameters remaining as is today, i.e., the key/cert being the same as they are in today\u0027s deployment. \nI can remove the default value for the keyfile and certfile and submit a patch if you think that makes sense.\nI dont think we should try to do insecure connection with ONOS if there is issue with key/cert file. Because, ONOS works either securely or insecurely, not both at a time.\nThoughts?",
      "parentUuid": "9a5c5d37_5538e69f",
      "revId": "c9b39b05aa317f5096823bb41d05ad1158fe5e9c",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
